\f0\fs24 \cf2 Look closely: the grotesque decoration running along the display cabinet in the Red Room is not just an elegant ornament\'85 it\'92s a subtle and refined tribute to one of the jewels of Venetian art: Santa Maria dei Miracoli. Yes, the stunning church adorned with marbles and decorations, designed by Pietro Lombardo and his sons in the late 15th century. Once again, the Bagatti Valsecchi brothers did not simply copy. They studied, reinterpreted, and translated that beauty into a new language, tailored to their home. They meticulously designed the motif \'96 literally, on graph paper \'96 and entrusted it to the expert hand of Innocente Cattaneo, who transferred it onto wood with masterful skill. The result? A decoration that combines erudition and craftsmanship, historical memory and contemporary creativity. Another piece in the great Renaissance mosaic that is this house.\
